# Agent-Bus Push Reminder

## Invariant

∀ assistant turn closure after reply/post to web-anthropic: **prefer CDP / operator-proxy / converse continuity to wake web** — report status only; **¬** ask the operator to push merely because an open thread expects web next.

Human push reminder is a **degraded path** so context can be removed/updated without the human as continuity hinge. Emit it **only when** autonomous CDP wake is unavailable or broken.

¬ mechanical: posting `--to web-anthropic` alone is insufficient (for either wake or reminder).

Wake mechanics: `claude-ai-cdp-navigation` · `cdp-operator-proxy` — this rule owns **turn-close reminder gating** only.

## Decision (apply after reply + thread-state update)

| Condition | Reminder? |
|---|---|
| Thread **closed** in same pass (`update-thread --status closed`, or ack-only closeout) | **No** — arc complete; push would deliver noise |
| CDP / `project_ask` / `team_dispatch(model=cdp/…)` / operator-proxy continuity **already waking** this thread (started or completed) | **No** — automation delivered the wake; operator nudge is false (friction 24628) |
| Thread **open** ∧ web expected next ∧ CDP wake **can** be fired (substrate available) | **No** — fire CDP wake; status report OK; **¬** human push cue |
| Thread **open** ∧ web expected next ∧ CDP wake **unavailable or broken** (dead CSE with no warm path; aborted poller with no reconnect; no CDP substrate; explicit operator-attended handoff that is not CDP-capable) | **Yes** — degraded path only |
| `post`/`reply` to non-web agents (`cursor`, `grok`, …) | **No** |
| Peek / fetch / read-only; thread-state write with no reply | **No** |

**Edge — open closeout to web:** leave thread open for web to read/close does **not** license a human push cue when CDP can wake. Same table: CDP first; reminder only if CDP wake unavailable/broken.

**`team_dispatch` `push_reminder` field:** server may still return a formatted string — **do not echo it** when the table says **No**. Echo only when the degraded-path row passes.

## Lead ordering invariant (a25444)

For any open web-anthropic leg that will use CDP on the **same** coordination thread:

1. Stage cortex corpus + sealed prompt
2. **`project_ask(op=submit, …)` / CDP `team_dispatch(model=cdp/…)` MUST complete before assistant turn close** (after answer-3 preflight + **required** bus pointer on arc coordination legs)
3. Turn closes **without** human push reminder (status report only)

**Falsifier (regression):** human push reminder emitted **and** CDP wake succeeded (or was available) on the same thread in the same leg → friction a25444 / steward-false-push class.

**Root cause (5403):** `team_dispatch` handoff returned `push_reminder` before CDP submit; seat echoed reminder at turn close. Gradual `/overhaul` steps 4 (deep) and 11 must **not** default to handoff path — use CDP per `overhaul.md` + `/review-arch-doc` default.

## Reminder format (when degraded-path gate passes)

> **Action needed — push to web-anthropic**: reply posted to thread {ID} turn {N}. Autonomous CDP wake unavailable — push the agent-bus message to trigger web-anthropic's turn.

## Targets (web side only)

- `scripts/agent-bus reply --to web-anthropic …`
- `scripts/agent-bus post --to web …` / `reply --to web …`
- `team_dispatch` handoff `push_reminder` in the response (same gate: open thread ∧ CDP unavailable → remind)
